            <h2>Section 3: China's Dental Implant Market in 2026 — What's Actually Happening</h2>

            <p>China's volume-based procurement (VBP) program, which began rolling out in 2023, was designed to make dental implants more affordable for domestic patients. The program works by the government acting as a single buyer and negotiating bulk pricing. By 2025, the program had driven down prices at public hospitals significantly.</p>

            <p>For international patients, the effect is indirect but real. Private hospitals catering to foreign patients now compete aggressively on price to attract medical tourists, since the VBP program has made domestic patients more price-sensitive. Straumann noted in their February 2026 earnings that China remains a "procurement uncertainty" — corporate speak for "we're still figuring out how this policy affects our pricing power."</p>

            <p>At the same time, 3D printed medical devices are becoming more common in Chinese dental clinics, which further reduces per-unit costs for custom abutments and surgical guides. The IndexBox market report (May 2026) shows China's 3D printed medical devices market growing, with dental applications being a significant segment.</p>

